window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["35"]={"https://theconversation.com/nobody-cared-new-research-shows-deepfakes-are-hurting-regular-people-not-just-celebrities-296154":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6255f95d39ff41432cfc626e714186b78e72a19507a4ab30badf54df40708c9e","read":"https://theconversation.com/nobody-cared-new-research-shows-deepfakes-are-hurting-regular-people-not-just-celebrities-296154","bytes":181124,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Nobody cared’: new research shows deepfakes are hurting regular people, not just celebrities","by":[{"n":"Nicola Henry","r":"Professor of Global & Language Studies, RMIT University"},{"n":"Gemma Stevens","r":"Research Assistant, School of Global, Urban and Social Studies, RMIT University"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T00:40:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In 2017, a ",["Reddit user","https://www.vice.com/en/article/gal-gadot-fake-ai-porn/"],", who went by the name “deepfakes”, shared non-consensual AI-generated videos of celebrities he’d created by “stitching” their faces onto the bodies of pornographic actors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nearly ten years later, AI tools can generate highly realistic sexualised “deepfake” images in seconds, sometimes using just a single photograph. Often, ",["high-profile people","https://www.esafety.gov.au/industry/tech-trends-and-challenges/deepfakes"]," are targeted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["recently published research","https://doi.org/10.1080/10447318.2026.2723677"]," – involving more than 7,000 people from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States – reveals AI-generated image-based abuse is becoming increasingly widespread. It now affects ordinary people as well as public figures."]},{"k":"h","s":["How are deepfakes made?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["AI-generated image-based sexual abuse","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/1369118X.2026.2613437"]," refers to the non-consensual creation, distribution, or threatened distribution of synthetic intimate images depicting real people. This is also known as “non-consensual sexual deepfakes”."]},{"k":"p","s":["With little technical skill required, almost anyone can create these images and almost anyone can become a target."]},{"k":"p","s":["These tools include ",["“nudify” apps","https://arxiv.org/html/2411.09751v1"]," that digitally remove clothing from photographs, as well as AI generators that create new images or manipulate existing images from text prompts or reference images."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia set to ban ‘nudify’ apps. How will it work?","https://theconversation.com/australia-set-to-ban-nudify-apps-how-will-it-work-264349"]]},{"k":"p","s":["These tools are accessible, easy to find and sometimes free, expanding the pool of potential victims and perpetrators, including young people."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to the ",["Australian eSafety Commissioner","https://www.esafety.gov.au/newsroom/media-releases/esafety-urges-schools-to-report-deepfakes-as-numbers-double"],", the number of reports from children involving digitally altered intimate images, including deepfakes, have more than doubled in the 18 months to June 2025 compared with the total number of reports received in the preceding seven years combined."]},{"k":"p","s":["Four in five of those reports involve girls."]},{"k":"h","s":["What our research found"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our team ",["surveyed 7,230 adults","https://doi.org/10.1080/10447318.2026.2723677"]," in Australia, the UK and the US in July 2024. We found 7% reported being victims of non-consensual sexual deepfakes, with higher rates among:"]},{"k":"li","s":["people under 35"]},{"k":"li","s":["LGBTQIA+ people"]},{"k":"li","s":["Black, Indigenous, and other people of colour"]},{"k":"li","s":["people with disabilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["men."]},{"k":"p","s":["The true prevalence is likely to be higher as many victim-survivors may never discover that images of them have been created or shared, while perpetrators may be reluctant to disclose their behaviour, even in an anonymous survey."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also found ",["3.2%","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0747563226000324"]," admitted to having created, shared or threatened to share AI-generated intimate images of someone else without their consent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perpetrators described a range of motivations, not all of which involved revenge or an explicit intention to cause harm. Some “thought it was funny”, while others wanted to “experiment with technology” or “show off” to friends and online peers."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings suggest deepfakes can occur within peer cultures where sexualised content is used for humour, social bonding or mockery, as well as humiliation and harassment."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the impacts?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most victim-survivors in our study reported anger, humiliation, shame, embarrassment, fear, helplessness and distress."]},{"k":"p","s":["While men were more likely to report victimisation, women were more likely to report a broader range of harms and negative emotional and social impacts. Men were more likely to find the experience funny, although these were a minority."]},{"k":"p","s":["The harms do not necessarily depend on how realistic the images appear to be. Victim-survivors can experience significant distress from losing control over how they are sexually represented. They can also experience fear others will believe the images are authentic, and the possibility of further humiliation or abuse."]},{"k":"p","s":["In our study, one participant said they felt fearful the perpetrator would “continue uploading” images and the abuse might escalate to in-person violence. Others worried sexualised material associated with their names could be discovered by prospective employers or others."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once images circulate, victims can face an exhausting “whack-a-mole” cycle of locating and reporting images, only for copies to reappear elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some victim-survivors also described being disbelieved or having their experiences minimised, including by authorities, friends and family members because the images were considered to be “not real”."]},{"k":"p","s":["As one young woman in the UK put it: “nobody cared, believed me or listened”."]},{"k":"p","s":["A young non-binary person, also in the UK, said:"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was kind of a level of scepticism from the people I told; because it wasn’t a ‘real image’ they couldn’t really see why I was so upset and thought it was less compromising because it wasn’t actually me in the picture."]},{"k":"h","s":["Prevention and accountability"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perpetrators must be held accountable. Prevention, however, cannot be left to individuals alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Technology companies must make their products and services safer and more resistant to misuse. This means building safeguards into AI tools to prevent abusive images being generated, making harmful content harder to find or circulate, and ensuring accessible reporting and rapid removal processes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The burden should not fall on victims to continually search for and report the material."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s proposed ",["digital duty of care","https://theconversation.com/australias-digital-duty-of-care-was-just-introduced-to-parliament-so-whats-in-the-bill-294464"],", introduced into parliament last month, is an important step forwards."]},{"k":"p","s":["This would require online services, including AI image-generation services, to take reasonable steps to keep users safe. It would also give the eSafety commissioner new powers to target nudify apps and websites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Going further, Australia could consider ",["following the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/crime-and-policing-act-2026-factsheets/crime-and-policing-act-2026-intimate-image-abuse-factsheet"]," in criminalising the development and supply of nudify tools."]},{"k":"p","s":["There should also be criminal offences for non-consensual sharing and creation of AI-generated intimate images in all states and territories."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also need consent-based and respectful relationships education which challenges the idea that creating sexualised images of others is harmless fun, and which works to address the gendered norms that normalise this behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Educational interventions","https://theconversation.com/mandatory-consent-education-is-a-huge-win-for-australia-but-consent-is-just-one-small-part-of-navigating-relationships-177456"]," need to also focus on fostering social connection and building healthy relationships."]},{"k":"p","s":["If this article has raised issues for you, call 1800RESPECT on 1800 737 732 or visit the eSafety Commissioner’s website for helpful online safety resources. You can also contact Lifeline crisis support on 13 11 14 or text 0477 13 11 14, Suicide Call Back Services on 1300 659 467, or Kids Helpline on 1800 55 1800 (for young people aged 5-25). If you or someone you know is in immediate danger, call the police on 000."]}],"chars":6341},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"9725206f01d82a43bfee5ffbf0106c7cc0c2fad672898f99ab90be9f1c12bb94","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia","bytes":79509,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bolivia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T14:58:18+00:00","mod":"2026-09-22T16:45:15+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Chapare region of Cochabamba Department including Villa Tunari and highway routes 4 and 24 that pass through Chapare."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["State of Emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["A State of Emergency has been declared in Bolivia, giving police and armed forces powers to remove roadblocks, disrupt protests and detain those not complying with the new measures for up to 8 hours without charge. Follow the advice of local authorities, be wary of unverified or unofficial information, stay alert and keep away from protests and roadblocks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and roadblocks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not try to cross roadblocks. The situation has the potential to deteriorate without warning. Allow extra time to reach your destination and make sure you are ready to change your plans quickly if needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any British national who requires urgent consular assistance, should contact us by phone on +44 (0)20 7008 5000, selecting the option: ‘Consular services for British nationals’. If you are in Bolivia and using a phone with a local SIM, please call 2-2010020."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel by Road"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (available inside Bolivia only) to see which roads are blocked."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you purchase a bus ticket ‘condicionado’ it means the bus company may not be able to guarantee arrival to your destination."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],". Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Bolivia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bolivia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Bolivian Embassy in the UK","https://bolivianembassy.co.uk/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bolivia, your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least two blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need to show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel or hostel booking and its address, at least for your first night in Bolivia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get an entry stamp when you arrive in Bolivia, otherwise you’ll have to pay a fine when you leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Bolivia overland, make sure you get your passport stamped on both sides of the border, with an exit stamp from the country you are leaving and an entry stamp on the Bolivian side."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia no longer stamps passports on the border with Argentina, but you must register your exit with Argentina’s immigration authorities (in Spanish) who pass the information to Bolivian immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy cannot intervene in immigration issues."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Bolivia for up to 90 days without a visa. Border officials issue 30-day stamps, but you can stay for 90 days without any new stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a tourist, you get 90 days of visa-free travel in a one-year period. If you want to stay longer, check with the ",["Bolivian Embassy in the UK","https://bolivianembassy.co.uk/"]," (in Spanish) or the ",["Department of Immigration","https://migracion.gob.bo/index.php/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["To work or study, for business travel or for other reasons, you must meet the Bolivian government’s entry requirements (in Spanish). Requirements include a police criminal record certificate from the UK, which you can get from the ",["ACRO Criminal Records Office","https://acro.police.uk/s/"],". If you need any documents from the UK, get them translated into Spanish and ",["legalised by the Legalisation Office","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["If only one parent or legal guardian is travelling with a child, you cannot visit Bolivia for longer than 90 days. If you stay for more than 90 days, the child will need a judicial permit to leave Bolivia with only one parent."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bolivia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bolivia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Bolivia","https://www.aduana.gob.bo/aduana7/content/viajero"]," (in Spanish). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. You should declare through ",["Bolivia’s 250 declaration form","https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=12b180b923e5007f8fdbbcd8b267ca6f06c33b30efbe1b0caa06c551e0985ba7JmltdHM9MTc1MzY2MDgwMA&ptn=3&ver=2&hsh=4&fclid=360c5dd0-5880-67e2-0ccc-49fa59f966a1&psq=bolivia+250+form&u=a1aHR0cDovL2FuYnN3MDEuYWR1YW5hLmdvYi5ibzo3NDAxL3ZpYWplcm8vUHVibGljbzI1MC5qc3A&ntb=1"]," (link only works in Bolivia)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Bolivia, terrorist attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia is experiencing an economic crisis and dollar shortage which has led to an increase in crime rates. Petty crime is common in central La Paz, in other popular tourist destinations, on buses and in crowded areas. Do not leave your bag or other belongings unattended. Always keep your passport, money and other valuable items in a safe place. On night buses, use a money belt under your clothes for important documents and credit cards; theft can occur when you are asleep."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminals impersonating Police Officers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves can impersonate police officers. They have used fake police ID cards, uniforms and even police stations to fool victims. They may ask to check your documents and your bags and take your belongings."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not get into an unmarked police car under any circumstances. The police cannot stop or search you on the street without a written order from a state prosecutor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in robberies from people taking taxis in Santa Cruz, La Paz and Rurrenabaque. If you use a taxi:"]},{"k":"li","s":["seek local advice and use established companies"]},{"k":"li","s":["order the taxi by phone – ‘radio taxis’ have the telephone number and the name of the taxi company on the roof"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for a sticker on the windscreen or windows – registered taxis should display one"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not get into a taxi already carrying other passengers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ignore anyone offering help at taxi stands and bus terminals and watch your belongings. Thieves work in teams to distract their victims."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Political Situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests, marches and demonstrations can occur with little prior notice. If they occur, you should move away from the area and remain in a safe place. Stay alert to developments and pay attention to instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protestors may block roads. Do not attempt to cross blockades in a motor vehicle or on a motorbike. Recent blockades have led to fuel and fresh food shortages in some areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce any risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings and protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and monitor local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["take the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of unverified, unofficial information"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow extra time to reach your destination"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal Kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists, especially those travelling alone, are at risk of ‘express kidnapping’ in Bolivia. These are short-term, opportunistic abductions aimed at extracting cash from the victim. Victims may be held hostage for up to several days while criminals use stolen bank or credit cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign visitors are particularly vulnerable when entering Bolivia at overland border points with Peru, Chile and Argentina. If you’re travelling from the town of Copacabana to La Paz, try to use a direct bus."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several incidents at the Cementerio General and the Sopocachi areas of La Paz."]},{"k":"p","s":["Express kidnappers sometimes impersonate police officers to target foreigners. They have used fake police ID cards, uniforms and even police stations to fool victims."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police cannot stop or search you on the street without a written order from a state prosecutor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings and always let someone you trust know your whereabouts, especially after dark. If you are a victim of kidnapping, follow the kidnapper’s instructions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been rape and sexual assault incidents at clubs and hostels. Be cautious if you’re approached by strangers. Lock your room when you return to your hotel or hostel."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Prison tours"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid prison tours. They’re illegal and unsafe. There are no guarantees for your safety inside prisons."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and immigration officials sometimes carry out ID checks. Carry copies of the photo page from your passport and the Bolivian entry stamps. Leave the original document in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal bars"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are illegal bars in Bolivia. If the police find you at one, you may be detained for questioning, particularly if drugs are found at the premises. Legal bars close at 3am."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia is the world’s third largest producer of cocaine. There are harsh penalties for those caught trafficking or in possession of drugs. The minimum sentence is 8 years and prison conditions are very poor. Never leave luggage unattended when departing the country and avoid any contact with illegal drugs. Under Bolivian law carrying any amount of illegal drugs or substances is considered drug trafficking."]},{"k":"p","s":["All passengers on departing international flights from Bolivia will have their hold and hand baggage searched by the Police Narcotics Division, and this will include a search of your person and your bags by a sniffer dog."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ayahuasca ceremonies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ayahuasca is a traditional plant used in ‘spiritual cleansing’ ceremonies by indigenous communities in Bolivia, primarily in the Amazon region, but also near La Paz. At these ceremonies people consume a brew containing dimethyltryptamine (DMT), a hallucinogenic drug that is a class A substance in the UK. It is not illegal to consume this brew, but its interaction with existing medical conditions is not well understood. People have suffered serious illnesses and in some cases death after consuming it. Some Ayahuasca retreats are in remote areas, making it difficult to get medical help."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in remote areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful travelling with cameras and binoculars in remote areas, particularly in coca-growing areas such as the Chapare and the Yungas, where people can be suspicious of anyone taking photographs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check before taking photographs of local people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal. However, same-sex relationships are frowned on by many Bolivians, more so in the Altiplano than in Santa Cruz, where attitudes tend to be more liberal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adventure activities in Bolivia include mountain biking, salt flat tours and jungle expeditions. There are no official minimum standards for tour operators. Get local advice and only use reputable companies. Check your travel insurance policy covers you for the activities you’re planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re mountain biking on the so-called ‘Death Road’, from La Paz to Coroico through the Yungas Valley, make sure the bikes are in good condition. Check your guide is carrying safety equipment and first-aid kit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular petrol and diesel shortages across the country with long queues forming at service stations in anticipation of deliveries. Bus services between cities may be affected due to lack of fuel and there may be less available public transport in La Paz and other major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bolivia, take these fuel shortages into account. They can make long distance travel difficult and strand those traveling by car for several days while waiting for fuel deliveries, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car to drive in Bolivia. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel can be dangerous due to poor road conditions and low driving standards. Serious accidents can happen on the main tourist routes. Some of Bolivia’s main highways are paved but most roads are unpaved rough tracks."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season (November to March) there is a risk of landslides and roads can be blocked. Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (in Spanish/accessible only from within Bolivia) and get local advice before you set out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicles are often not well maintained. Four-wheel drive vehicles are often needed, especially during the rainy season. Broken-down vehicles with no warning lights are a frequent hazard on roads at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Accidents involving public transport, especially long-distance buses, are common and have affected British nationals. Bus drivers drive for longer than would be permitted under UK laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many taxis and most bus companies do not meet UK standards and rarely have seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards for bus transportation around Bolivia vary greatly between providers. Please keep safety in mind when booking your transportation. Some bus companies which cater specifically for the tourist market, although they may be more expensive, tend to have better safety standards, including seatbelts and better trained drivers. You should research the type of bus you will be taking carefully before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road blockades"]},{"k":"p","s":["A State of Emergency was declared in Bolivia on 21 June to restrict protests and blockades. Protest groups often use road blockades as a form of protest, without warning. Avoid large crowds and demonstrations, and do not attempt to cross blockades. Blockades can disrupt public transport at very short notice. Protests or demonstrations may result in widespread road blockades, including on roads to and from airports. Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (in Spanish) to see which roads are blocked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of Bolivia’s airports lack safety and rescue capability. Airports outside the departmental capitals are less likely to possess fire and rescue equipment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lake and river travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The boat trips on Lake Titicaca offer boats that are often very basic. The same is true of boats used for river excursions in jungle areas. Check life jackets are provided."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones%22%20/t%20%22_blank"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest fires are common during the dry season (May to October) and affect some parts of Southern and Eastern Bolivia. This can impact air quality in the areas most affected by the fires but also in other parts of the country, including La Paz. It is advisable to wear a face mask if the air quality is particularly bad, or to stay inside."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding, landslides and snowfall"]},{"k":"p","s":["Floods and landslides are common, particularly in mountainous areas during the rainy season (November to March), although weather can be unpredictable throughout the year. Roads can become impassable for days at a time. Travellers may become stranded in high, remote areas. Take food, water and warm clothing with you in case of delays or bad weather."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes can happen in Bolivia, although serious earthquakes are rare. Many buildings, particularly older buildings and those outside major cities, may not be built to withstand earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re affected by an earthquake:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re indoors, stay inside and take cover under a sturdy piece of furniture or against an interior wall, away from windows"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re outdoors, move away from buildings, trees and power lines"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of the risk of aftershocks"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should familiarise yourself with general earthquake safety advice before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional Risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Bolivia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Chapare Region of Cochabamba Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Chapare region of Cochabamba Department. This includes Villa Tunari and highway routes 4 and 24 that pass through Chapare. This is due to a high level of gang-related violent crime predominantly linked to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is difficult for the British Embassy to provide in-person emergency or consular support in these areas. Local authorities may also be very limited in the help they can provide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 118 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public healthcare in Bolivia can be inconsistent in response times and quality of service throughout the country. In remote areas the provision of emergency medical assistance is limited. Consider private alternatives if they are available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccination recommendations for Bolivia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Bolivia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Oropouche virus disease"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Bolivia, including in La Paz and the Salar de Uyuni salt flats. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some medications are currently in short supply in Bolivia. If you take prescription medicine, please ensure you have enough medicine to cover your stay in Bolivia. You must bring your prescription with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["The public healthcare system does not meet the same standards as the UK, and you may not be able to access the public health system as it is already overstretched. Bolivia is also prone to shortages in medical supplies and pharmaceuticals. There are private clinics in all main cities that work with international insurance. It is very important to have travel insurance and access to funds, as you will need to pay up front to receive treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 119"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Bolivia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Bolivia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Bolivia"]," in Bolivia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bolivia/british-embassy-la-paz"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-bolivia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21988,"change":"Updated information about the State of Emergency ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/canadas-international-student-cap-hit-atlantic-universities-hard-heres-why-it-matters-295649":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"0ab36aa7a66214ee0c03ceabee9cd268ed717bb74794df0955e3d889edae3c21","read":"https://theconversation.com/canadas-international-student-cap-hit-atlantic-universities-hard-heres-why-it-matters-295649","bytes":184287,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Canada’s international student cap hit Atlantic universities hard. Here’s why it matters","by":[{"n":"Dale Kirby","r":"Professor, Faculty of Education, Memorial University of Newfoundland"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T12:10:44Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["Canada’s efforts to reduce international student numbers","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/media-room/international-student-program-reforms-controlled-growth-fell-short-improving-integrity.html"]," have had a striking effect in Atlantic Canada. Universities in the region have lost nearly half their international students in three years."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to ",["preliminary figures released in October","https://atlanticuniversities.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/web_AAU-enrolment-press-release-Oct-12-FINAL-EN_FR.pdf"],", international enrolment fell by 3,020 students (18 per cent) in the past year. That brings the decline since federal restrictions began in January 2024 to almost 48 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s restrictions aim to address national concerns, but their effects vary across the country. The sharp decline in Atlantic Canada raises questions about whether federal policy takes enough account of smaller provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["International students cap falsely blames them for Canada’s housing and health-care woes","https://theconversation.com/international-students-cap-falsely-blames-them-for-canadas-housing-and-health-care-woes-221859"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A decline beyond expectations"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, Ottawa ",["introduced a cap","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2024/01/canada-to-stabilize-growth-and-decrease-number-of-new-international-student-permits-issued-to-approximately-360000-for-2024.html"]," on international student study permit applications. The government cited rapid growth, housing pressures and concerns about oversight."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government subsequently ",["set further limits","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/notices/2026-provincial-territorial-allocations-under-international-student-cap.html"]," on international student enrolments for 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["There were good reasons for reform. International student recruitment had grown quickly, and governments needed to ensure that institutions could support the students they admitted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the scale and distribution of the decline have surprised even federal officials."]},{"k":"p","s":["In March, ",["Canada’s Auditor General reported","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/our-work/audit-reports/auditor-general-report-2026-international-student-program-reforms.html"]," that the restrictions had reduced new study permit approvals more sharply than expected. Ottawa anticipated declines of no more than 10 per cent in several smaller provinces, including all four Atlantic provinces. It even expected an increase in Newfoundland and Labrador. Instead, approvals fell by at least 59 per cent in these provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["The federal immigration department could not explain why approval rates fell so far below expectations. Allocating study permit applications to provinces does not guarantee that students will receive permits, accept university offers or enrol."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor can the entire enrolment decline be blamed on the federal cap. Student applications, permit approval rates, financial pressures and Canada’s appeal as a study destination also affect enrolment."]},{"k":"h","s":["The scene at Memorial University"]},{"k":"p","s":["Where I work in the faculty of education at Memorial University in Newfoundland, international enrolment ",["fell from 4,889 students in 2023 to 2,682 in fall 2026","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/newfoundland-labrador/mun-international-students-decline-9.7389650"],", a decrease of more than 45 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are signs of improvement. New international enrolment increased by 14 per cent this fall. But rebuilding student numbers after several years of decline will take time."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["an October update","https://gazette.mun.ca/teaching-and-learning/enrolment-update-2"],", Memorial reported that total enrolment had fallen by two per cent over the past year. This happened despite increases in new undergraduate and graduate students. Memorial’s experience shows how changes in immigration policy can make long-term university planning more difficult."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why regional differences matter"]},{"k":"p","s":["Atlantic Canada faces circumstances that differ greatly from Canada’s large metropolitan centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["A recent ",["Atlantic Economic Panel report","https://aep-peca.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/AEP-Full-Report-compressed-2.pdf"]," identifies an aging population and ongoing difficulties finding workers as barriers to economic growth. It also highlights the importance of immigration in sustaining population growth and addressing labour shortages."]},{"k":"p","s":["International students are not a substitute for sound immigration or workforce development policies. Not all international graduates choose to remain in Canada. Those who wish to stay must find suitable employment and meet immigration requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nevertheless, post-secondary education can provide a pathway into the Canadian workforce. International students in Atlantic Canada can develop professional networks, gain local work experience and build careers in the region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Falling international enrolment also affects university finances. ",["Statistics Canada reports","https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/250910/cg-d003-png-eng.htm"]," that international undergraduates paid an average of $41,746 in tuition in 2025–26. Canadian undergraduates paid an average of $7,734."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although fees vary by province and program, declining international enrolment can disproportionately affect university budgets. ",["It’s been estimated","https://higheredstrategy.com/the-state-of-post-secondary-education-in-canada-2026"]," that Canadian universities lost about $1 billion in annual international tuition revenue between 2023-24 and 2025-26. Further losses are projected through 2030-31."]},{"k":"p","s":["That doesn’t mean universities should depend indefinitely on international tuition to balance their budgets. Heavy reliance on one revenue source ",["leaves institutions vulnerable when policies change","https://press.insciencepress.org/index.php/press/catalog/view/38/48/744-1"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A better way to assess the policy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Addressing the enrolment decline doesn’t mean returning to the previous approach to international student recruitment. Concerns about housing, student protection and the integrity of the study permit process are important."]},{"k":"p","s":["But reducing study permit numbers should not be the only measure of success. The federal government should examine why approval rates differ so sharply among provinces. It should also consider regional needs and whether universities can adequately support international students."]},{"k":"p","s":["Provincial governments and universities have responsibilities too. These include providing housing and student services, maintaining sound recruitment practices and helping graduates find employment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Canada identifies international students as ‘ideal immigrants’ but supports are lacking","https://theconversation.com/canada-identifies-international-students-as-ideal-immigrants-but-supports-are-lacking-191105"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada needs policies that balance immigration goals with the unique needs of its regions. This doesn’t mean abandoning national limits; it means examining their effects and making changes where needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Atlantic Canada’s experience shows that reducing international student numbers is not enough to judge whether a policy works. Its impacts on universities, students and the communities they serve matter too."]}],"chars":5660},"https://theconversation.com/terpaksa-nyawit-di-tengah-karhutla-buruh-perempuan-menanggung-beban-berlapis-294942":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"5fab880166d39be54d1b95ec6fff58d5162a5a32c6bb6bb913573572107f2fca","read":"https://theconversation.com/terpaksa-nyawit-di-tengah-karhutla-buruh-perempuan-menanggung-beban-berlapis-294942","bytes":178803,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Terpaksa ‘nyawit’ di tengah karhutla, buruh perempuan menanggung beban berlapis","by":[{"n":"Hariati Sinaga","r":"Assistant Professor, Universitas Indonesia"}],"pub":"2026-10-28T08:29:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Buruh perempuan sawit terpaksa bekerja di tengah karhutla agar tetap mendapatkan upah."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Di tengah kepungan asap, perempuan menanggung risiko kesehatan dan biayanya secara mandiri."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Beban adaptasi bencana memperberat kerja domestik dan produktif perempuan tanpa kompensasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika kebakaran hutan dan lahan (karhutla) melanda sejumlah wilayah di Indonesia, perhatian publik banyak tertuju pada kerusakan hutan, kematian satwa, dan dampak asap terhadap kesehatan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, ada kelompok yang kerap luput dari pembahasan: buruh perkebunan sawit, terutama perempuan, yang harus tetap bekerja di tengah kepungan asap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dari pengamatan rutin dan mendengar cerita langsung dari lima orang buruh perempuan di Kalimantan Barat, saya menemukan kenyataan miris: mereka tetap harus bekerja meskipun asap pekat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi mereka, asap menciptakan dilema luar biasa. Berhenti bekerja bisa berarti kehilangan upah. Sementara itu, tetap bekerja berarti menghadapi risiko kesehatan yang belum tentu diimbangi perlindungan memadai dari perusahaan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tetap bekerja meski asap pekat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di perkebunan sawit, ",["buruh dengan status Syarat Kerja Utama (SKU)","https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-68944-5_9?"]," memiliki hubungan kerja yang relatif lebih tetap. Namun, mereka tetap dituntut memenuhi target. Buruh sawit SKU ini boleh cuti, tapi tidak selalu mudah digunakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Situasi lebih sulit sebenarnya dialami buruh harian lepas (BHL) kebun sawit, yang umumnya tidak memperoleh cuti (alias libur tetap dibayar), termasuk ketika sakit. Pekerja harian inilah yang sebenarnya menjadi tulang punggung industri sawit nasional karena jumlahnya diperkirakan mencapai ",["70% dari seluruh buruh perkebunan sawit","https://www.betahita.id/berita/11823/rambo-kepada-presiden-prabowo-buruh-sawit-paling-miskin"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sayangnya, banyak buruh perempuan bekerja di perkebunan sawit dengan ",["status BHL","https://online-journal.unja.ac.id/jseb/id/article/view/24542"],". Akibatnya, ketika memilih tidak bekerja karena asap terlalu pekat atau kondisi tubuh memburuk, mereka harus menanggung kehilangan pendapatan hari itu. Pilihannya menjadi sulit: menjaga kesehatan atau memastikan kebutuhan rumah tangga tetap terpenuhi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan status BHL, buruh perempuan bergantung pada upah harian yang dihitung berdasarkan Hari Kerja (HK). ",["Studi menunjukkan bahwa buruh perempuan dengan status BHL mendapatkan upah di bawah upah minimum, bahkan tidak cukup untuk memenuhi kebutuhan hidup mereka","https://indonesianfeministjournal.org/index.php/IFJ/article/view/886/544"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian di Kapuas Hulu, Kalimantan Barat","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1389934121002884?via%3Dihub"],", menunjukkan keterlibatan perempuan dalam perkebunan sawit berkaitan dengan meningkatnya waktu kerja produktif mereka, sekaligus berkurangnya waktu untuk beristirahat, tidur, dan menikmati waktu luang. Temuan ini menunjukkan bahwa beban kerja perempuan tidak berhenti ketika jam kerja selesai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi karhutla, kerentanan tersebut menjadi semakin berat. Bagi buruh perempuan yang sedang hamil, paparan asap juga berisiko mengganggu kesehatan janin."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian mengenai kebakaran hutan Indonesia","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6431162/"]," menemukan hubungan antara paparan polusi udara selama masa kehamilan dan gangguan pertumbuhan anak hingga usia remaja. Temuan ini memperlihatkan bahwa dampak asap dapat berlangsung jauh setelah api padam."]},{"k":"h","s":["Masker dibeli dengan uang sendiri"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sayangnya, kewajiban bekerja saat karhutla tidak selalu disertai perlindungan memadai. Seorang buruh perempuan suatu perkebunan sawit di Kalimantan Barat bercerita kepada saya bahwa perusahaan hanya menyediakan masker pada awal terjadinya karhutla 2026. Setelah itu, ia harus membeli masker sendiri untuk melindungi diri dari asap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman ini memperlihatkan bagaimana biaya menghadapi bencana dapat dialihkan dari perusahaan kepada buruh. Mereka tetap dituntut bekerja, tetapi harus mengeluarkan uang sendiri untuk mengurangi risiko kesehatan di tempat kerja."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam melakukan kerja perkebunan sawit sehari-hari, buruh perempuan perkebunan sawit ",["menghadapi paparan racun","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/15487733.2025.2532213#abstract"]," melalui bahan agrokimia dan air yang tercemar, yang kemudian berdampak pada kesehatan mereka. Situasi ini diperparah dengan bencana karhutla yang menimbulkan asap beracun yang dihirup oleh buruh perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kerentanan tersebut sejalan dengan ",["catatan Organisasi Perburuhan Internasional (ILO) pada 2024","https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/eliminating-vulnerability-female-workers-exploitation-palm-oil-and"],", yang menyoroti keterbatasan perlindungan keselamatan dan kesehatan kerja, jaminan sosial, serta upah yang layak bagi perempuan di sektor perkebunan sawit. Status kerja yang tidak tetap membuat akses mereka terhadap perlindungan semakin terbatas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pekerjaan belum selesai ketika pulang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beban buruh perempuan tidak berakhir setelah meninggalkan perkebunan. Ketika anggota keluarga jatuh sakit akibat paparan asap, perempuan sering kali menjadi pihak yang bertanggung jawab merawat mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada saat yang sama, pekerjaan rumah tangga seperti memasak, membersihkan rumah, dan mengurus anak tetap harus dilakukan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Buruh perempuan juga dapat dilibatkan perusahaan dalam pekerjaan tambahan, termasuk membantu memadamkan api di area perkebunan. Pekerjaan ini menambah risiko dan beban tenaga, terutama jika tidak disertai perlindungan maupun upah tambahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan demikian, ongkos karhutla bukan hanya biaya membeli masker atau pengobatan. Ada pula waktu istirahat yang hilang, pendapatan yang berkurang, dan pekerjaan perawatan yang tidak dibayar."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Riset","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1389934121002884?via%3Dihub"]," menunjukkan bahwa keterbatasan waktu dan berkurangnya waktu istirahat merupakan bagian penting dari dampak sosial perkebunan sawit terhadap perempuan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Perlindungan buruh tak boleh terpisah dari penanganan karhutla"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman buruh perempuan menunjukkan bahwa penanganan karhutla tidak cukup hanya berfokus pada pemadaman api dan pemulihan lingkungan. Perlindungan terhadap orang-orang yang bekerja di wilayah terdampak juga harus menjadi prioritas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam beberapa kasus, perusahaan perkebunan menyediakan layanan cek kesehatan kepada para pekerjanya. Selain dapat digunakan untuk memantau kondisi kesehatan buruh perempuan, hasil cek kesehatan ini dapat menjadi dokumentasi penting tentang risiko kesehatan bawaan yang dimiliki buruh perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perusahaan perlu menyediakan masker yang sesuai dengan risiko paparan, fasilitas kesehatan, dan prosedur kerja yang mengutamakan keselamatan. Buruh juga harus memiliki perlindungan pendapatan ketika kondisi berbahaya membuat pekerjaan tidak aman dilakukan. Pemerintah perlu memastikan hak ketenagakerjaan tersebut benar-benar diterapkan, termasuk bagi buruh harian lepas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada saat yang sama, layanan kesehatan dan dukungan bagi keluarga terdampak perlu diperkuat agar beban perawatan tidak terus dibebankan kepada perempuan. Dalam jangka panjang, upaya mencegah kebakaran dan membatasi ekspansi perkebunan monokultur ke kawasan hutan juga penting untuk mengurangi risiko ekologis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karhutla memang membakar lahan dan merusak ekosistem. Namun, dampaknya juga terasa dalam kehidupan sehari-hari buruh yang harus terus bekerja, mengeluarkan uang untuk melindungi diri, lalu pulang untuk merawat keluarga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tanpa perubahan dalam perlindungan kerja dan pembagian beban perawatan, perempuan akan terus menanggung ongkos bencana yang jauh lebih besar daripada yang terlihat di balik kepulan asap."]}],"chars":6830}};
